{"title":"2015 CEMC Euclid Problems/Problem 2b","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2015 CEMC Euclid Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_2b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Two circles have the same centre. The radius of the smaller circle is 1. The area of the region between the circles is equal to the area of the smaller circle.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_2b&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>What is the radius of the larger circle?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_2b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Area\" title=\"Area\">area</a> of a circle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/e/88e1ac9b59dc367092dad4ca13e35ab3442551ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi r^{2}$\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />. Since the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Radius\" title=\"Radius\">radius</a> of the smaller circle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, its area must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/a/b8ab25b93e8df9d001296ceca3c283ce48d0b06c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi \\times 1^{2} = \\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"87\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Since the area of the region between the two circles is equal to the area of the smaller <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Circle\" title=\"Circle\">circle</a>, its area must also be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ca003a7da0de4994b4733e203b74ff52d42553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" />. This means that the total area of the large circle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/2/ac2dbcb2ce9e7ee0a1e14b43667c132a342b92a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi + \\pi = 2\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"90\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the radius of the larger circle. This means that:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/b/9abdc019fdaa27c93c40b9334b833fe19931f502.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi R^{2} = 2\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"79\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/e/66e4dbc27f51f031705eec5cf81a49705203f21c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R^{2} = \\frac{2 \\pi}{\\pi} = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"105\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/0/47027ffe09dbb8e0c222acd29b6158c6bdf55306.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R = \\pm \\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"78\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/1/3b1b4ecc23bb68d80371eb4fdb99f91633b4db8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R = \\boxed {\\sqrt{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"76\" height=\"32\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/6/296b1846c4f21e2c1237486740c79e9bebd064ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018000314\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.014 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.023 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 51/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 491/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1957/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.249      1 -total\n 48.45%    5.935      1 2015_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_2\n 42.56%    5.213      1 Template:Image_needed\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36017:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018000314 and revision id 279635. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}